9318	{"artifactId":"LLD-f9ced66a0e8835b8-s1","entry":{"id":"migrated-LLD-f9ced66a0e8835b8-s1-review","actor":{"id":"insrc:daemon","kind":"agent","properties":{}},"timestamp":"2026-10-08T07:52:31.699Z","operation":"review","outcome":{"result":"pass","summary":"review: pass","data":{"kind":"review","report":{"artifact":"design.story","stage":"design.story","verdict":"pass","findings":[{"claimId":"fix-targets-defect.1","ref":"fix-targets-defect","item":"fix-targets-defect","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The design narrows BOTH consumers of the Story's range — the subject's changed set (changedFiles' committed-range branch) and the degraded grounding's rangeDiff — to the Story's own change units, and adds the reviewer cwd fix. Together these cover both root causes the ISSUE names.","evidence":"ISSUE rootCause (1) names the base..HEAD range read by resolveStoryRangeBase and assembleDiffCodeReviewGrounding; (2) names CliProvider.complete calling runClaude(args, prompt) with no exec override. In the code, the subject's changed set comes from changedFiles (subject.ts:114-126, which passes the range base), and that function's committed branch is `collectDiff(repoPath, { from: opts.base, ...globs }, ranged)` (changed-files.ts:144). The grounding range is `rangeDiff(...) { return runDiff(repoPath, { from: base, ...excludeInput(excludeGlobs) }) }` (grounding.ts:364-366). The design changes all three sites (2.3, 2.4, 2.7-2.9). The fix intent's 'merge committed on its own' part is enforced by the merge-in-progress gate (2.10) plus the prompt rule (2.11). Fast-forward and committed-squash integrations are a declared known limit that tests pin; they are not silently dropped. [files: src/workflow/code-review/subject.ts, src/workflow/runners/build/changed-files.ts, src/workflow/code-review/grounding.ts, .insrc/artifacts/ISSUE-f9ced66a0e8835b8.json]","action":"None. The known limits are stated and pinned by tests; consider surfacing them to the user at approval.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"current-behaviour.1","ref":"current-behaviour","item":"current-behaviour","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Today CliProvider.complete and completeStructuredOnce call runClaude/runCodex without an ExecOverride, so the subprocess inherits the daemon's cwd, even though runClaude/runCodex already accept {cwd, timeoutMs}.","evidence":"cli-provider.ts:170 `await this.runClaude(args, prompt)`, :177 `await this.runCodex(args, prompt)`, :263 and :278 likewise. Meanwhile `private runClaude(args, prompt, exec?: ExecOverride)` → `runSubprocess(..., exec?.timeoutMs ?? this.timeoutMs, exec?.cwd)` (:445-447, :464-465), and the ExecOverride interface carries `cwd?` (:529-530). [files: src/agent/providers/cli-provider.ts]","action":"None.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"current-behaviour.2","ref":"current-behaviour","item":"current-behaviour","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Today the clean-tree review range is one net base..HEAD diff, so a mid-build merge's files enter both the changed set and the bounded hunk body.","evidence":"grounding.ts:246 `if (b !== undefined && deps.rangeDiff !== undefined) return deps.rangeDiff(repoPath, b, g);` → runDiff {from: base} → git_diff argv `git diff <from>..HEAD` (diff.ts:220-224). changed-files.ts:142-145 does the same for the path set. buildDiffSymbols uses splitDiffByFile(diff.body), so a truncated body yields `[no hunk text for …]` (grounding.ts:281-287), matching the ISSUE's observation (b). [files: src/workflow/code-review/grounding.ts, src/workflow/runners/build/changed-files.ts, src/daemon/tools/builtins/git/diff.ts]","action":"None.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"change-sites.1","ref":"change-sites","item":"change-sites","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The five dimension judges (adherence, conventions, coverage, functional-coverage, quality) are the code-review's only provider calls, each one completeStructured call, and subject.repoPath is available to pass as cwd.","evidence":"A grep of src/workflow/code-review (non-test) for completeStructured|complete( finds exactly five calls: adherence.ts:147, conventions.ts:156, coverage.ts:172, functional-coverage.ts:149, quality.ts:132. The subject is built as `{ repoPath, epicHash, storyId, changedFiles, ... }` (subject.ts:144). [files: src/workflow/code-review/dimensions/adherence.ts, src/workflow/code-review/dimensions/conventions.ts, src/workflow/code-review/dimensions/coverage.ts, src/workflow/code-review/dimensions/functional-coverage.ts, src/workflow/code-review/dimensions/quality.ts, src/workflow/code-review/subject.ts]","action":"None.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"change-sites.2","ref":"change-sites","item":"change-sites","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The merge gate sites handleImplement / handleValidate exist and can gate before any prompt render or record write, including the standalone path that renders renderStandaloneImplementPrompt.","evidence":"handleImplement (src/mcp/build-step/phases/implement.ts:42) resolves repoPath first (:45). It then branches early to handleStandaloneImplement (:53-55), before noteBuildStart (:74) and renderImplementPrompt (:87). handleValidate is at validate.ts:140. A gate placed right after resolveRepoPath therefore covers both the plan and standalone paths. One detail matters: the gate must go BEFORE the standalone early return, or standalone builds escape it. The git_diff inputSchema has `additionalProperties: false` (diff.ts:82), so `paths` must also be added to that schema. Both edits are in files the design already lists. [files: src/mcp/build-step/phases/implement.ts, src/mcp/build-step/phases/validate.ts, src/daemon/tools/builtins/git/diff.ts]","action":"In the plan, place the mergeInProgress check immediately after resolveRepoPath (before the standalone branch), and add `paths` to gitDiffTool.inputSchema.properties.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"preserved-behaviour.1","ref":"preserved-behaviour","item":"preserved-behaviour","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Ledger exclusion is done by git through git_diff's exclude (LEDGER_EXCLUDE_GLOBS) for the review set and grounding, while the BUILD changeLog uses exact-path exclusions only. Keeping exclude on every per-unit call and intersecting after git's exclusion therefore preserves both.","evidence":"changed-files.ts:55-60 defines LEDGER_EXCLUDE_GLOBS, forwarded as `{ exclude: [...opts.excludeGlobs] }` to every diff (:122-128, :144). Before the git_diff call, pathspecArgs emits `:(top,exclude,glob)` entries (diff.ts:203-207). validate.ts:363-366 calls collectBuildChangeLog with `exclude: [own.json, own.md, buildStartRelPath(...)]` and base, with no globs, and collectBuildChangeLog forwards only base/exclude (changed-files.ts:188-191). The design intersects with storyChangeSet.paths after the existing git-excluded diff and before `keep`, so the exclusion order is unchanged. [files: src/workflow/runners/build/changed-files.ts, src/daemon/tools/builtins/git/diff.ts, src/mcp/build-step/phases/validate.ts]","action":"None.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"preserved-behaviour.2","ref":"preserved-behaviour","item":"preserved-behaviour","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The range-base invariants hold: the first stamp wins (CR-3) and resolveStoryRangeBase returns the stamp's rangeBase first. The design does not touch either.","evidence":"gates.test.ts:365 `test('CR-3: re-approving after the work has landed does NOT move rangeBase forward — the FIRST stamp wins'`. The design rejects a3 (moving the base) and consumes the base unchanged in storyChangeSet(repoPath, base). Neither range-base.ts nor noteBuildStart (implement.ts:74) is in its change sites. [files: src/workflow/__tests__/gates.test.ts, src/workflow/runners/build/range-base.ts]","action":"None.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"tests.1","ref":"tests","item":"tests","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Each acceptance criterion maps to at least one test that would fail without the fix, and the existing CR-3 regression test it cites for ac4 is real.","evidence":"ac1: 'a clean tree with a base reports only the Story's own files, not files a merge brought in' and 'the range diff carries full hunks for the Story files and none for merged-in files' both fail today, because changedFiles/rangeDiff return the whole base..HEAD set (changed-files.ts:144, grounding.ts:365). ac2: mergeInProgress / build-step 'merge-in-progress' tests fail today because no such gate exists in implement.ts. ac3: 'every code-review dimension judge passes the reviewed repoPath as cwd' fails today because judges call completeStructured with no opts (e.g. adherence.ts:147). ac4: regression guards, including the existing CR-3 test at gates.test.ts:365. [files: src/workflow/__tests__/gates.test.ts, src/workflow/code-review/dimensions/adherence.ts, src/mcp/build-step/phases/implement.ts]","action":"None.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"}],"counts":{"high":0,"med":0,"low":8,"unverified":0},"template":"design-issue","reviewedAt":"2026-10-08T07:52:31.699Z","model":"cli-claude:opus","reviewedBy":"daemon"},"resolutions":{}}}}}
